        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "edea13b2-47e5-5473-a81e-19b69d17c971",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vinko Knežević, Vincent Knesevich de Szent-Helena\n- Places: County of Tyrol, Graz, Marengo\n- Organizations: Habsburg Monarchy, Austrian Empire, Holy Roman Empire, Austria-Hungary\n- Roles: Croatian nobleman, general\n- Events: Battle of Marengo\n\nFacts:\n- The County of Tyrol was established about 1140 as a state of the Holy Roman Empire.\n- In 1804, the Princely County of Tyrol was unified with the secularised Prince-Bishoprics of Trent and Brixen and became a crown land of the Austrian Empire.\n- In 1805, Vinko Knežević led Austrian Empire troops in the Tyrol.\n- In 1809, Vinko Knežević led Austrian Empire troops at Graz.\n- From 1867, the County of Tyrol was a Cisleithanian crown land of Austria-Hungary.\n- Vinko Knežević, also known as Vincent Knesevich de Szent-Helena, was born on 30 November 1755 and died on 11 March 1832.\n- Vinko Knežević was a Croatian nobleman and a general in the imperial army service of the Habsburg Monarchy.\n- Vinko Knežević commanded an infantry brigade at Marengo the year after an earlier referenced event.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0d116857-dcd7-56dd-aafa-ade9d294a7d0",
        "text": "Page: Vinko Knežević. Sentence: Vinko Knežević or Vincent Knesevich de Szent-Helena (30 November 1755 – 11 March 1832) was a Croatian nobleman and general in the Habsburg Monarchy imperial army service.\nPage: Vinko Knežević. Sentence: He commanded an infantry brigade at Marengo the following year and led Austrian Empire troops in the Tyrol in 1805 and at Graz in 1809.\nPage: County of Tyrol. Sentence: The Princely County of Tyrol, until 1493: County of Tyrol, was a State of the Holy Roman Empire established about 1140.\nPage: County of Tyrol. Sentence: In 1804 the Princely County of Tyrol, unified with the secularised Prince-Bishoprics of Trent and Brixen, became a crown land of the Austrian Empire in 1804 and from 1867 a Cisleithanian crown land of Austria-Hungary.",
